    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\angle OCB=90^\\circ-x$; base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal; $\\angle COB=2x$; $\\angle BAC=x$.",
      "worked": "$\\angle OCB=90^\\circ-x$ because $OC$ is perpendicular to the tangent.\n\n$OB=OC$, so $\\angle OBC=90^\\circ-x$ because base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\angle COB&=180^\\circ-(90^\\circ-x)-(90^\\circ-x)\\\\\\angle COB&=2x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe angle at the centre is double the angle at the circumference standing on the same arc:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\angle BAC&=\\frac{2x}{2}\\\\\\angle BAC&=x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore $\\angle BCQ=\\angle CAB$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
